th> and <math alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are similar, but not whether they are congruent.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangles <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, angles <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper E\"><mi>E</mi>\n</math> each have measure <math alttext=\"27 degree\"><mrow><mn>27</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and angles <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper F\"><mi>F</mi>\n</math> each have measure <math alttext=\"41 degree\"><mrow><mn>41</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to determine whether triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is congruent to triangle <math alttext=\"upper D upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"ce3b6f4f-60f0-4503-b733-4d7804f8a14b","templateid":"b09d9bfc-9539-49c5-bd53-ec0a19db85dc","vaultid":"ef5d400f-0428-4fec-9dbc-0c4f61cd3559","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"33cafaba-ced2-4a53-b6c7-e62aa66d1db0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5f9abd1e-dcbf-43e4-9dbc-f9d4f75edb4e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The length of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4756032-6811-4916-b00a-5257ebdab04e","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The lengths of sides <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper E upper F\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>E</mi>\n\t<mi>F</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"af834fc5-b7ca-400e-8921-214e83046e6b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">No additional information is necessary.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959838,"updateDate":1691007959838}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959838, 1691007959838),
    ($SATQ$901e3285$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$028920-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span>, the measure of angle <span class="italic">A</span> is <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_004_59d66db9.png" alt="50 degrees"></span></span>. If triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> is isosceles, which of the following is NOT a possible measure of angle <span class="italic">B </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_000_59d66db9.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_001_dccd8204.png\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_002_fde77410.png\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_003_2c7e08f2.png\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The sum of the three interior angles in a triangle is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_005_429202ed.png" alt="180 degrees"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class="italic">A</span> measures <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_006_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>. If angle <span class="italic">B</span> measured <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_007_2c7e08f2.png" alt="100 degrees"></span>, the measure of angle <span class="italic">C</span> would be <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_008_5d752093.png" alt="180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 100 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 30 degrees"></span>. Thus, the measures of the angles in the triangle would be <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_009_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_010_2c7e08f2.png" alt="100 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_011_44dd7f9a.png" alt="30 degrees"></span>. However, an isosceles triangle has two angles of equal measure. Therefore, angle <span class="italic">B</span> can&rsquo;t measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_012_2c7e08f2.png" alt="100 degrees"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. If angle <span class="italic">B</span> has measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_013_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, then angle <span class="italic">C</span> would measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_014_8545f924.png" alt="180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 80 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_015_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_016_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_017_fde77410.png" alt="80 degrees "></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice B is incorrect. If angle <span class="italic">B</span> has measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_018_dccd8204.png" alt="65 degrees"></span>, then angle <span class="italic">C</span> would measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_019_5467d595.png" alt="180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 65 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 65 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_020_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_021_dccd8204.png" alt="65 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_022_dccd8204.png" alt="65 degrees"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice <span class="italic">C</span> is incorrect. If angle <span class="italic">B</span> has measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_023_fde77410.png" alt="80 degrees"></span>, then angle <span class="italic">C</span> would measure <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_024_9522eb13.png" alt="180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 80 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 50 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_025_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_026_fde77410.png" alt="80 degrees"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_027_f5492eee.png" alt="50 degrees"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 28, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"901e3285","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"028920-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span>, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span> is <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_004_59d66db9.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span></span>. If triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is isosceles, which of the following is NOT a possible measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">B </span>?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_000_59d66db9.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_001_dccd8204.png\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_002_fde77410.png\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_003_2c7e08f2.png\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The sum of the three interior angles in a triangle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_005_429202ed.png\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_006_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> measured <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_007_2c7e08f2.png\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_008_5d752093.png\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 100 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 30 degrees\"></span>. Thus, the measures of the angles in the triangle would be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_009_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_010_2c7e08f2.png\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_011_44dd7f9a.png\" alt=\"30 degrees\"></span>. However, an isosceles triangle has two angles of equal measure. Therefore, angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> can&rsquo;t measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_012_2c7e08f2.png\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_013_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_014_8545f924.png\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 80 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_015_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_016_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_017_fde77410.png\" alt=\"80 degrees \"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice B is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_018_dccd8204.png\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_019_5467d595.png\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 65 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 65 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_020_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_021_dccd8204.png\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_022_dccd8204.png\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice <span class=\"italic\">C</span> is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_023_fde77410.png\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_024_9522eb13.png\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 80 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 50 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_025_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_026_fde77410.png\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/901e3285/img_027_f5492eee.png\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":28,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959623,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"901e3285","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959623,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"028920-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"6f8813f1-d617-407a-87b3-5e93df655257","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"028920-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span>, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span> is <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span></span>. If triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is isosceles, which of the following is NOT a possible measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">B </span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p><span class=\"choice_cell align:right \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The sum of the three interior angles in a triangle is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees\"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> measured <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 100 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 30 degrees\"></span>. Thus, the measures of the angles in the triangle would be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"30 degrees\"></span>. However, an isosceles triangle has two angles of equal measure. Therefore, angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> can&rsquo;t measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"100 degrees\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 50 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 80 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"80 degrees \"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice B is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 65 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 65 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"65 degrees\"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle. Choice <span class=\"italic\">C</span> is incorrect. If angle <span class=\"italic\">B</span> has measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span>, then angle <span class=\"italic\">C</span> would measure <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees minus, open parenthesis, 80 degrees plus 50 degrees, close parenthesis, equals 50 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"80 degrees\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"50 degrees\"></span> could be the angle measures of an isosceles triangle.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959623,"updateDate":1691007959623}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959623, 1691007959623),
