$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Triangles <span class="italic">ABC</span> and <span class="italic">DEF</span> are shown above. Which of the following is equal to the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_005_5320e955.png" alt="B C over A, B"></span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_000_56088dfd.png\" alt=\"D E over D F\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_001_f5bd0890.png\" alt=\"D F over D E\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_002_086b5bad.png\" alt=\"D F over E F\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_003_516ce562.png\" alt=\"E F over D E\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. In right triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span>, the measure of angle <span class="italic">B</span> must be 58&deg; because the sum of the measure of angle <span class="italic">A</span>, which is 32&deg;, and the measure of angle <span class="italic">B</span> is 90&deg;. Angle <span class="italic">D</span> in the right triangle <span class="italic">DEF</span> has measure 58&deg;. Hence, triangles <span class="italic">ABC</span> and <span class="italic">DEF</span> are similar (by angle-angle similarity). Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_006_db819a7e.png" alt="side B C"></span> is the side opposite to the angle with measure 32&deg; and <span class="italic">AB</span> is the hypotenuse in right triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span>, the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_007_5320e955.png" alt="the length of side B C over the length of side A, B"></span> is equal to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_008_f5bd0890.png" alt="the length of side D F over the length of side D E"></span>.<p>Alternate approach: The trigonometric ratios can be used to answer this question. In right triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span>, the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_009_799c12f2.png" alt="the length of side B C over the length of side A, B equals, the sine of 32 degrees"></span>. The angle <span class="italic">E</span> in triangle <span class="italic">DEF</span> has measure 32&deg; because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_010_b96b01e8.png" alt="the measure of angle D, plus the measure of angle E, equals 90 degrees"></span>. In triangle <span class="italic">DEF</span>, the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_011_af876da0.png" alt="the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals the sine of 32 degrees"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_012_2e96830c.png" alt="the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals, the length of side B C over the length of side A, B"></span>.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_013_56088dfd.png" alt="the length of side D E over the length of side D F"></span> is the reciprocal of the ratio <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_014_5320e955.png" alt="the length of side B C over the length of side A, B"></span>. Choice C is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_015_53aa136e.png" alt="the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals the length of side B C over the length of side A, C"></span>, not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_016_5320e955.png" alt="the length of side B C over the length of side A, B"></span>. Choice D is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_017_b3135e62.png" alt="the length of side E F over the length of side D E, equals, the length of side A, C over the length of side A, B"></span>, not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/933fee1a/img_018_5320e955.png" alt="the length of side B C over the length of side A, B"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
