>ABC</span>, the ratio <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side B C over the length of side A, B equals, the sine of 32 degrees\"></span>. The angle <span class=\"italic\">E</span> in triangle <span class=\"italic\">DEF</span> has measure 32&deg; because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the measure of angle D, plus the measure of angle E, equals 90 degrees\"></span>. In triangle <span class=\"italic\">DEF</span>, the ratio <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals the sine of 32 degrees\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals, the length of side B C over the length of side A, B\"></span>.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side D E over the length of side D F\"></span> is the reciprocal of the ratio <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side B C over the length of side A, B\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side D F over the length of side D E, equals the length of side B C over the length of side A, C\"></span>, not <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of side B C over the length of side A, B\"></span>. Choice 