<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the figure shown, <math alttext="line segment upper B upper C"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext="line segment upper A upper D"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext="x equals 22"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>22</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Line <math alttext="t"><mi>t</mi>
</math> passes through points <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper C"><mi>C</mi>
</math>. What is the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4c7f320e-c664-43c3-af37-2e089c7741a6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9a014842-9c60-45c5-b29a-8df05cbf9da0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2341a988-6fb6-42e8-a52d-a7c9122445ee","content":"<p><math alttext=\"158\"><mn>158</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It's given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="line segment upper B upper C"><menclose notation="top"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></menclose></math> is parallel to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="line segment upper A upper D"><menclose notation="top"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></menclose></math>. Since line <em><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math></em> intersects <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="line segment upper B upper C"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="line segment upper A upper D"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, it's a transversal. The angles in the figure marked as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math>&deg; and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>&deg; are on opposite sides of the transversal and lie between the parallel segments, so they are alternate interior angles. When two parallel segments are intersected by a transversal, alternate interior angles have equal measure. It's also given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 22"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="22"><mn>22</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2 x"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, not the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the complement of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="22"><mn>22</mn></math>, not the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the supplement of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="22"><mn>22</mn></math> , not the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9342ca50","external_id":"2d07d31c-7627-4c6e-813d-60c0e28346b7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"0e81d428-6b81-4008-a3d8-8ad7a2d41b71","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg id=\"uuid-8b73b37f-24bf-4e22-ba48-c766ce033bb7\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"363.647\" height=\"178.496\" viewBox=\"0 0 363.647 178.496\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quadrilateral upper A upper B upper C upper D. Refer to long description.\"><path d=\"m70.208,174.896v-.63h.195c.23,0,.437-.025.623-.075.185-.05.332-.152.442-.308.11-.155.165-.388.165-.697v-7.351c0-.3-.058-.522-.173-.667-.115-.146-.265-.24-.45-.285s-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h2.745l5.37,8.295v-6.646c0-.3-.058-.522-.172-.667-.115-.146-.265-.24-.45-.285s-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h3.765v.63h-.195c-.22,0-.425.025-.615.075s-.34.149-.45.3c-.11.149-.165.385-.165.705v9h-1.065l-5.625-8.641v6.931c0,.31.055.542.165.697.11.155.26.258.45.308s.395.075.615.075h.195v.63h-3.765Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m85.389,175.046c-1.08,0-1.93-.345-2.55-1.034-.62-.69-.93-1.74-.93-3.15,0-1.4.297-2.442.892-3.128.595-.685,1.473-1.027,2.633-1.027,1.08,0,1.93.343,2.55,1.027.62.686.93,1.728.93,3.128,0,1.41-.298,2.46-.893,3.15-.595.689-1.473,1.034-2.632,1.034Zm.03-.779c.5,0,.9-.128,1.2-.383.3-.255.515-.638.645-1.147.13-.51.195-1.135.195-1.875,0-1.12-.155-1.96-.465-2.521-.31-.56-.84-.84-1.59-