346.189-.743.284-1.192.284Zm.015-.885c.41,0,.728-.125.952-.375.226-.25.338-.585.338-1.005,0-.43-.115-.77-.345-1.02-.23-.25-.546-.375-.945-.375-.39,0-.703.125-.938.375-.235.25-.353.59-.353,1.02,0,.42.115.755.345,1.005.23.25.545.375.945.375Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><line x1=\".342\" y1=\"138.213\" x2=\"355.916\" y2=\"8.795\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line><polyline points=\"35.242 126.099 46.396 19.993 325.035 19.993\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"2\"></polyline><polyline points=\"324.935 19.982 332.963 125.993 35.035 125.993\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"2\"></polyline></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for quadrilateral upper A upper B upper C upper D\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>Line t passes through points upper A and upper C.</li>\n<li>The measure of angle upper A upper C upper B is x°.</li>\n<li>The measure of angle upper C upper A upper D is y°.</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure shown, <math alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> is parallel to <math alttext=\"line segment upper A upper D\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext=\"x equals 22\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>22</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> passes through points <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4c7f320e-c664-43c3-af37-2e089c7741a6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9a014842-9c60-45c5-b29a-8df05cbf9da0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2341a988-6fb6-42e8-a52d-a7c9122445ee","content":"<p><math alttext=\"158\"><mn>158</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></menclose></math> is parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper D\"><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></menclose></math>. Since line <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math></em> intersects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper D\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, it's a transversal. The angles in the figure marked as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>&deg; and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>&deg; are on opposite sides of the transversal and lie between the parallel segments, so they are alternate interior angles. When two parallel segments are intersected by a transversal, alternate interior angles have equal measure. It's also given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 22\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 x\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the complement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math>, not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the supplement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math> , not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"9342ca50","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"2d07d31c-7627-4c6e-813d-60c0e28346b7","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"0e81d428-6b81-4008-a3d8-8ad7a2d41b71","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg id=\"uuid-8b73b37f-24bf-4e22-ba48-c766ce033bb7\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"363.647\" height=\"178.496\" viewBox=\"0 0 363.647 178.496\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quadrilateral upper A upper B upper C upper D. Refer to long description.\"><path d=\"m70.208,174.896v-.63h.195c.23,0,.437-.025.623-.075.185-.05.332-.152.442-.308.11-.155.165-.388.165-.697v-7.351c0-.3-.058-.522-.173-.667-.115-.146-.265-.24-.45-.285s-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h2.745l5.37,8.295v-6.646c0-.3-.058-.522-.172-.667-.115-.146-.265-.24-.45-.285s-.388-