nt upper A upper D\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext=\"x equals 22\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>22</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Line <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> passes through points <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"43e1ece0-f3f8-4413-9a9c-38db4aacb3c4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4c7f320e-c664-43c3-af37-2e089c7741a6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9a014842-9c60-45c5-b29a-8df05cbf9da0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"68\"><mn>68</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2341a988-6fb6-42e8-a52d-a7c9122445ee","content":"<p><math alttext=\"158\"><mn>158</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></menclose></math> is parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper D\"><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></menclose></math>. Since line <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math></em> intersects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper B upper C\"><mover><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"line segment upper A upper D\"><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, it's a transversal. The angles in the figure marked as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math>&deg; and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>&deg; are on opposite sides of the transversal and lie between the parallel segments, so they are alternate interior angles. When two parallel segments are intersected by a transversal, alternate interior angles have equal measure. It's also given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 22\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 x\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the complement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math>, not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the supplement of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math> , not the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>","externalid":"2d07d31c-7627-4c6e-813d-60c0e28346b7","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
    ($SATQ$93de3f84$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$05721-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The volume of right circular cylinder&nbsp;A is 22&nbsp;cubic centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of a right circular cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder&nbsp;A?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>11</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>22</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>44</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>66</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The volume of right circular cylinder A is given by the expression <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_000_c51c04dc.png" alt="pi r squared times h"></span>, where <span class="italic">r </span>is the radius of its circular base and <span class="italic">h</span> is its height. The volume of a cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder A is given by <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_001_5cb32938.png" alt="pi times, open parenthesis, 2 r, close parenthesis, squared, times one half h"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_002_ccd2f2f3.png" alt="4 pi r squared, times, one half h, and equals 2 pi r squared times h"></span>. Therefore, the volume is twice the volume of cylinder A, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_003_16e83f22.png" alt="2 times 22, equals 44"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and likely results from not multiplying the radius of cylinder A by 2. Choice B is incorrect and likely results from not squaring the 2 in 2<span class="italic">r </span>when applying the volume formula. Choice D is incorrect and likely results from a conceptual error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"93de3f84","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"05721-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The volume of right circular cylinder&nbsp;A is 22&nbsp;cubic centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of a right circular cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder&nbsp;A?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>11</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>22</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>44</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>66</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The volume of right circular cylinder A is given by the expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_000_c51c04dc.png\" alt=\"pi r squared times h\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">r </span>is the radius of its circular base and <span class=\"italic\">h</span> is its height. The volume of a cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder A is given by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_001_5cb32938.png\" alt=\"pi times, open parenthesis, 2 r, close parenthesis, squared, times one half h\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_002_ccd2f2f3.png\" alt=\"4 pi r squared, times, one half h, and equals 2 pi r squared times h\"></span>. Therefore, the volume is twice the volume of cylinder A, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/93de3f84/img_003_16e83f22.png\" alt=\"2 times 22, equals 44\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and likely results from not multiplying the radius of cylinder A by 2. Choice B is incorrect and likely results from not squaring the 2 in 2<span class=\"italic\">r </span>when applying the volume formula. Choice D is incorrect and likely results from a conceptual error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":4,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959629,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"93de3f84","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1691007959629,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"05721-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"bae829cd-8d20-4d9a-9554-433ce11f45f5","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"05721-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The volume of right circular cylinder&nbsp;A is 22&nbsp;cubic centimeters. What is the volume, in cubic centimeters, of a right circular cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder&nbsp;A?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>11</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>22</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>44</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>66</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The volume of right circular cylinder A is given by the expression <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi r squared times h\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">r </span>is the radius of its circular base and <span class=\"italic\">h</span> is its height. The volume of a cylinder with twice the radius and half the height of cylinder A is given by <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"pi times, open parenthesis, 2 r, close parenthesis, squared, times one half h\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 pi r squared, times, one half h, and equals 2 pi r squared times h\"></span>. Therefore, the volume is twice the volume of cylinder A, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 times 22, equals 44\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and likely results from not multiplying the radius of cylinder A by 2. Choice B is incorrect and likely results from not squaring the 2 in 2<span class=\"italic\">r </span>when applying the volume formula. Choice D is incorrect and likely results from a conceptual error.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959629,"updateDate":1691007959629}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959629, 1691007959629),
    ($SATQ$93f48423$SATQ$, $SATQ$05f34b6c-f496-4574-bc7b-cffaaa469975$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">What is the area, in square inches, of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> inches and a width of <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> inches?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6e0c9ad2-6fbf-4b97-845f-43fb3ac60bbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8a7e4eb9-d73e-4e74-8bc3-e7829bf2de0d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b6477c7d-555c-4e03-bcd7-e33a071c33f3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The area, <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>, of a rectangle is given by the formula <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> represents the length of the rectangle and <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> represents its width. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> inches and a width of <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> in the formula <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="upper A equals 42"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>42</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Thus, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math alttext="42"><mn>42</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum, not the product, of the length and width of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"93f48423","external_id":"05f34b6c-f496-4574-bc7b-cffaaa469975","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"0df8a010-7169-4b26-a044-1e68e18a5315","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the area, in square inches, of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> inches?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6e0c9ad2-6fbf-4b97-845f-43fb3ac60bbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8a7e4eb9-d73e-4e74-8bc3-e7829bf2de0d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b6477c7d-555c-4e03-bcd7-e33a071c33f3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area, <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, of a rectangle is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> represents the length of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> represents its width. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 42\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>42</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum, not the product, of the length and width of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357406,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"93f48423","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1730147357406,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"05f34b6c-f496-4574-bc7b-cffaaa469975","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"0df8a010-7169-4b26-a044-1e68e18a5315","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"6e0c9ad2-6fbf-4b97-845f-43fb3ac60bbf"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"8a7e4eb9-d73e-4e74-8bc3-e7829bf2de0d"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"b6477c7d-555c-4e03-bcd7-e33a071c33f3"}],"externalid":"05f34b6c-f496-4574-bc7b-cffaaa469975","keys":["eae86035-c3a5-43d7-a320-3b9809091f01"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The area, <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, of a rectangle is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> represents the length of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> represents its width. It&rsquo;s given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> inches. Substituting <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 6 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 42\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>42</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum, not the product, of the length and width of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the area, in square inches, of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> inches?</p>","type":"mcq","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1730147357406,"updateDate":1730147357406}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357406, 1730147357406),
    ($SATQ$94364a79$SATQ$, $SATQ$2a19ba5d-f615-44cf-bbf1-badb5fc9d6f7$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$9c3bb4fb-36fc-43f5-8529-b995fd41067c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Two nearby trees are perpendicular to the ground, which is flat. One of these trees is <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> feet tall and has a shadow that is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> feet long. At the same time, the shadow of the other tree is <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> feet long. How tall, in feet, is the other tree?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6e273cee-794d-491f-af6d-01865f8f588d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e7f9a269-76eb-466a-8da3-79723849073e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8efcead6-d96b-42f2-a6a9-4c0bae3a0992","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"265f503d-2a6f-4431-9381-484b41df648d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e7f9a269-76eb-466a-8da3-79723849073e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. Each tree and its shadow can be modeled using a right triangle, where the height of the tree and the length of its shadow are the legs of the triangle. At a given point in time, the right triangles formed by two nearby trees and their respective shadows will be similar. Therefore, if the height of the other tree is <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, in feet, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> can be calculated by solving the proportional relationship <math alttext="StartFraction 10 feet tall Over 5 feet long EndFraction equals StartFraction x feet tall Over 2 feet long EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;tall</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;long</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;tall</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;long</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. This equation is equivalent to<math alttext="StartFraction 10 Over 5 EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="2 equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of the equation <math alttext="2 equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="4 equals x"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Therefore, the other tree is&nbsp;<math alttext="4 feet"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></math> tall.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from calculating the difference between the lengths of the shadows, rather than the height of the other tree.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from calculating the difference between the height of the <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>-foot-tall tree and the length of the shadow of the other tree, rather than calculating the height of the other tree.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from a conceptual or calculation error.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"94364a79","external_id":"2a19ba5d-f615-44cf-bbf1-badb5fc9d6f7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"9c3bb4fb-36fc-43f5-8529-b995fd41067c","uId":"23b79d46-3d44-4137-96b6-94374de3bffd","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Two nearby trees are perpendicular to the ground, which is flat. One of these trees is <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> feet tall and has a shadow that is <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> feet long. At the same time, the shadow of the other tree is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> feet long. How tall, in feet, is the other tree?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6e273cee-794d-491f-af6d-01865f8f588d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e7f9a269-76eb-466a-8da3-79723849073e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8efcead6-d96b-42f2-a6a9-4c0bae3a0992","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"265f503d-2a6f-4431-9381-484b41df648d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["e7f9a269-76eb-466a-8da3-79723849073e"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Each tree and its shadow can be modeled using a right triangle, where the height of the tree and the length of its shadow are the legs of the triangle. At a given point in time, the right triangles formed by two nearby trees and their respective shadows will be similar. Therefore, if the height of the other tree is <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>, in feet, the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> can be calculated by solving the proportional relationship <math alttext=\"StartFraction 10 feet tall Over 5 feet long EndFraction equals StartFraction x feet tall Over 2 feet long EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;tall</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;long</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;tall</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet&#160;long</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math>. This equation is equivalent to<math alttext=\"StartFraction 10 Over 5 EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"2 equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying each side of the equation <math alttext=\"2 equals StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"4 equals x\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Therefore, the other tree is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"4 feet\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext></math> tall.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from calculating the difference between the lengths of the shadows, rather than the height of the other tree.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from calculating the difference between the height of the <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math>-foot-tall tree and the length of the shadow of the other tree, rather than calculating the height of the other tree.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from a conceptual or calculation error.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959837,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"94364a79","skill_c