<mi>A</mi>
<mi>B</mi>
<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math> are <math alttext="54 degree"><mn>54</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>, <math alttext="90 degree"><mn>90</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>,&nbsp;and <math alttext="left parenthesis StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis degree"><mfenced><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. It follows that <math alttext="54 plus 90 plus StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 180"><mn>54</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or <math alttext="144 plus StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 180"><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="144"><mn>144</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 36"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="k equals 72"><mrow>
<mi>k</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>72</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="72"><mn>72</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction"><mrow>
<mfrac>
<mi>k</mi>
