mi>B</mi>\n<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> are <math alttext=\"54 degree\"><mn>54</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>, <math alttext=\"90 degree\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math>,&nbsp;and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&deg;</mo></math>. It follows that <math alttext=\"54 plus 90 plus StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 180\"><mn>54</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"144 plus StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 180\"><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"144\"><mn>144</mn>\n</math> from each side of this equation yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction equals 36\"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"k equals 72\"><mrow>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>72</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"StartFraction k Over 2 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>k</mi>\n<mn>2</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"05a3c218-67ad-4fcc-a95c-61a1756c68c5","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1743430554979,"updateDate":1743430554979}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554979, 1743430554979),
    ($SATQ$96467fea$SATQ$, $SATQ$22accec5-7fd4-4bbf-8af1-a6077fe56fc3$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Circle N has a radius of <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> millimeters <math alttext="left parenthesis mm right parenthesis"><mfenced><mtext>mm</mtext></mfenced></math>. Circle M has an area of&nbsp;<math alttext="64 pi m m squared"><mn>64</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. What is the total area, in <math alttext="m m squared"><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circles N and M?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"946af175-35d4-4b72-aa41-414df0b027bb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"113 pi\"><mn>113</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"4702924f-05d7-4b1a-98ac-399e261023e9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"92 pi\"><mn>92</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"96149cb0-61a2-452a-9829-6fb214c44d7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"78 pi\"><mn>78</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"509713e7-ca35-49cd-83f8-44f4de5df662","content":"<p><math alttext=\"15 pi\"><mn>15</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["946af175-35d4-4b72-aa41-414df0b027bb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that circle N has a radius of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7"><mn>7</mn></math> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="mm"><mtext>mm</mtext></math>. The area of a circle is given by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="pi r squared"><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius of the circle. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7"><mn>7</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> in the expression yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="pi left parenthesis 7 right parenthesis squared"><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49 pi"><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, for the area, in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="mm Superscript 2"><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circle N. It&rsquo;s also given that the area of circle M is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="64 pi"><mn>64</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="mm Superscript 2"><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Adding the two areas&nbsp;yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="49 pi plus 64 pi"><mn>49</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="113 pi"><mn>113</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="mm Superscript 2"><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the total area, in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="mm Superscript 2"><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circles N and M is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="113 pi"><mn>113</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect&nbsp;and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"96467fea","external_id":"22accec5-7fd4-4bbf-8af1-a6077fe56fc3","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"1ce23c3c-71db-4971-999e-8a0239b7dfc3","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Circle N has a radius of <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> millimeters <math alttext=\"left parenthesis mm right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mtext>mm</mtext></mfenced></math>. Circle M has an area of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"64 pi m m squared\"><mn>64</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. What is the total area, in <math alttext=\"m m squared\"><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circles N and M?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"946af175-35d4-4b72-aa41-414df0b027bb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"113 pi\"><mn>113</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"4702924f-05d7-4b1a-98ac-399e261023e9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"92 pi\"><mn>92</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"96149cb0-61a2-452a-9829-6fb214c44d7a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"78 pi\"><mn>78</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"509713e7-ca35-49cd-83f8-44f4de5df662","content":"<p><math alttext=\"15 pi\"><mn>15</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>"}],"keys":["946af175-35d4-4b72-aa41-414df0b027bb"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that circle N has a radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"mm\"><mtext>mm</mtext></math>. The area of a circle is given by the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathM